theory.intro:
A point in space needs three numbers, written as the ordered triple $(x,y,z)$. The $x$-, $y$- and $z$-axes are at right angles to each other and meet at the origin. To reach a point, go along $x$, then across $y$, then up $z$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(-2.4,-2.4) node[below left,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.8,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.6) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$z$};
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$O$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (0,0)--(-1.5,-1.5) node[midway,right,font=\footnotesize]{$x$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (-1.5,-1.5)--(2.5,-1.5) node[midway,below,font=\footnotesize]{$y$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (2.5,-1.5)--(2.5,0.5) node[midway,right,font=\footnotesize]{$z$};
\fill (2.5,0.5) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (2.5,0.5) {$P(x,\,y,\,z)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Write the coordinates of $P$. The dashed construction path follows the $x$, $y$ and $z$ directions in order.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x={(0.6cm,-0.4cm)},y={(1cm,0cm)},z={(0cm,1cm)},every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (0,0,0)--(4,0,0);
\draw[->] (0,0,0)--(0,5,0);
\draw[<->] (0,0,-3)--(0,0,3);
\path (4,0,0) node[below] {$x$} (0,5,0) node[right] {$y$} (0,0,3) node[above] {$z$} (0,0,0) node[above left] {$O$};
\draw[dashed] (0,0,0)--(3,0,0)--(3,2,0)--(3,2,-2);
\path (1.5,0,0) node[below left] {$3$} (3,1,0) node[above] {$2$} (3,2,-1) node[right] {$2$};
\fill[black] (3,2,-2) circle (2pt);
\path (3,2,-2) node[below right] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Move $2$ units along the positive $x$-axis, then $3$ units parallel to the positive $y$-axis, then $1$ unit down parallel to the $z$-axis.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x={(0.6cm,-0.4cm)},y={(1cm,0cm)},z={(0cm,1cm)},every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (0,0,0)--(3.5,0,0);
\draw[->] (0,0,0)--(0,5,0);
\draw[<->] (0,0,-2)--(0,0,2.5);
\path (3.5,0,0) node[below] {$x$} (0,5,0) node[right] {$y$} (0,0,2.5) node[above] {$z$} (0,0,0) node[above left] {$O$};
\draw[dashed] (0,0,0)--(2,0,0)--(2,3,0)--(2,3,-1);
\path (1,0,0) node[below left] {$2$} (2,1.5,0) node[above] {$3$} (2,3,-0.5) node[right] {$1$};
\fill[black] (2,3,-1) circle (2pt);
\path (2,3,-1) node[below right] {$A(2,3,-1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

